# Declared-not-hosted entries: flake | attribute | kind | reason | file.
#
# One line per app or check a repository flake declares that no workflow
# step runs or builds. The declared-checks-hosted census fails on any
# entry whose attribute no longer exists, that is in fact hosted, whose
# reason is empty or of no allowed class, or whose class demands a
# citation, a live job id or a marker line it does not carry. Allowed
# classes:
#   retired: ...                       cites the classification and its
#                                      reason in offchain/nix/component-inventory.nix
#   hosted under another name: ...     names a declared job identifier
#                                      (one whitespace-separated token
#                                      equal to a workflow job id)
#   pending wiring: #<issue>, ...      a real test that cannot be wired
#                                      yet; valid only while the named
#                                      issue is open (the census reads the
#                                      state from the file handed to it).
#                                      Closed membership: only the
#                                      release-review check and default apps
#                                      with issue #565 are admitted.
#   tool: ...|<file>                   a runnable check marked as a tool:
#                                      never cited as evidence, allowed to
#                                      stay local (operator ruling of
#                                      2026-10-12). The fifth field names
#                                      the repository-relative path of the
#                                      file that defines the tool and must
#                                      carry the one-line marker
#                                      `Tool, not a guarantee: <purpose>`;
#                                      the census fails the entry when the
#                                      file is missing, lacks the marker
#                                      line, or is cited in the published
#                                      text in either citation form (the
#                                      command form `.#<attribute>` or the
#                                      path of that file).
.|cli-recovery-controls|app|hosted under another name: every part this composite serialises is judged in its own hosted job (cli-recovery-accepting, cli-recovery-lost-answer, cli-recovery-killed with the history and rollback steps, and the cli-recovery-cross-wallet-part matrix); the composite itself exceeds the receipt cap and this ticket's recovery-partition slice retires it
.|cli-recovery-cross-wallet|app|hosted under another name: the cli-recovery-cross-wallet-part matrix job runs every discovered cross-wallet case this composite serialises, each on its own node
.|default|app|tool: the local documentation site server (the same wrapper as docs-serve)|nix/docs.nix
.|demo1-cli-attach|app|hosted under another name: the demo1-attach-part matrix job runs each part this composite serialises (demo1-cli-attach-takes through demo1-cli-attach-over-allowance), each with its own registry and node
.|docs-serve|app|tool: the local documentation site server for reviewing the built site without publishing it|nix/docs.nix
.|publish-docs-boundary-test|app|hosted under another name: the publication-boundary job runs the publication-boundary-controls app, which exercises this same recorded publisher (the unchanged nix/release.nix definition with gh replaced by a recorder) through its positive and mutated cases
.|browser|check|hosted under another name: the browser job runs the browser-check app, the same checker body this check's sandbox executes
.|coverage|check|hosted under another name: the coverage job runs the coverage-check app, the same checker body this check's sandbox executes
.|docs|check|hosted under another name: the rendered-docs job runs the docs-check app, the same checker body this check's sandbox executes (a bare nix build of .#docs reaches the site package, not this check)
.|inventory|check|hosted under another name: the inventory job runs the inventory-check app, the same checker body this check's sandbox executes
.|model|check|hosted under another name: the model job runs the model-check app, the same checker body this check's sandbox executes
.|release|check|hosted under another name: the release-check job runs the release-check app, the same checker body this check's sandbox executes
.|simulator|check|hosted under another name: the simulator job runs the simulator-check app, the same checker body this check's sandbox executes
offchain|cage-test-vectors|app|hosted under another name: the registry-test-vectors job builds checks.x86_64-linux.cage-test-vectors, whose sandbox executes this app's binary in its JSON mode
offchain|connected-verifier|app|retired: classified unverified in offchain/nix/component-inventory.nix under #282 (imports the removed stateRepPolicyBytes accessor and expects the removed representative-policy blueprint; repair owned by #282, no required workflow consumes it)
offchain|li01|app|retired: classified unverified in offchain/nix/component-inventory.nix under #172 (D6-retired Naming Your Assets journey; journey/li01/Main.hs sets removed CageConfig fields cfgRepPolicy/cfgConsumerPin)
offchain|li-refusals|app|retired: classified unverified in offchain/nix/component-inventory.nix under #172 (D6-retired Naming Your Assets journey; journey/li-refusals/Main.hs references identifiers removed by #157)
offchain|naming-rows|app|retired: classified unverified in offchain/nix/component-inventory.nix under #172 (D6-retired Naming Your Assets journey, the lmlc runner; retired by the current-required-use criterion, no required consumer)
offchain|recovery-rows|app|retired: classified unverified in offchain/nix/component-inventory.nix under #172 (D6-retired Naming Your Assets journey; journey/recovery/Main.hs imports registerConsumerImpl, removed by 9cba521)
offchain|register-rows|app|retired: classified unverified in offchain/nix/component-inventory.nix under #283 (not on the D6 retired list; #283 owns its migration or retirement; journey/register/Main.hs imports registerConsumerImpl, removed by 9cba521)
offchain|repair-rows|app|retired: classified unverified in offchain/nix/component-inventory.nix under #172 (D6-retired Naming Your Assets journey; journey/repair/Main.hs imports registerConsumerImpl, removed by 9cba521)
offchain|retirement-rows|app|retired: classified unverified in offchain/nix/component-inventory.nix under #172 (D6-retired Naming Your Assets journey; journey/retirement/Main.hs imports registerConsumerImpl, removed by 9cba521)
offchain|retirement-verify|app|retired: classified unverified in offchain/nix/component-inventory.nix under #172 (D6-retired retained exhibit of the retirement journey; retired by the current-required-use criterion, no required consumer)
offchain|singular|app|hosted under another name: the demo1-archive job runs this packaged command line from the extracted release archive (the archive assembly builds ./offchain#singular, this app's program, and the journey drives it as separate singular processes)
offchain|cage-tests|check|hosted under another name: the journey job's focused off-chain suite step runs the cage-tests app, the same wrapped test binary this check executes in its sandbox
offchain|cage-tests-e2e|check|hosted under another name: the e2e-part matrix jobs run .#cage-tests-e2e, this same wrapped derivation, one lane per job
offchain|library|check|hosted under another name: the offchain-component-build job builds .#component-build, whose member paths include this library derivation (build only: no test executes)
offchain|lint|check|hosted under another name: the offchain-lint job runs .#lint, this same writeShellApplication derivation (apps.lint is checks.lint)
offchain|record-value-tests|check|hosted under another name: the naming-validators job runs the record-value-tests app, the same test binary this check executes with the naming blueprint pinned in its sandbox
conformance|conformance-tests|app|hosted under another name: the conformance-checks, conformance-budget, conformance-batch and conformance-book jobs each run one chapter of this harness (appendix tests, fold budget regression, batch instructions, the book) through the conformance and fold-budget-regression apps
conformance|conformance-exe|check|hosted under another name: every conformance job that runs the conformance app builds this executable inside its wrapper's closure; the check itself builds the executable only (build only: no test executes)
conformance|conformance-tests|check|hosted under another name: the conformance-checks job's unit-test step runs the conformance-appendix-tests app, the same test binary this check executes in its sandbox
conformance|coverage-gate-snapshot|check|hosted under another name: the coverage-gate job's frozen-snapshot step builds packages.coverageGateSnapshot, this same derivation
conformance|coverage-gate-tests|check|hosted under another name: the coverage-gate job's gate-test-suite step builds packages.coverageGateTests, this same derivation
conformance|format-check|check|hosted under another name: the format-check job runs the format-check app, the same body this check's sandbox executes
conformance|hlint-check|check|hosted under another name: the format-check job's hlint step runs the hlint-check app, the same body this check's sandbox executes
applications/open-datum/offchain|open-datum|app|hosted under another name: the registry-two-actors-replay-fault job builds and drives this application CLI (nix build of applications/open-datum/offchain#open-datum is the control's setup)
applications/open-datum/offchain|singular-negative|app|hosted under another name: the negative-host-ordinary, negative-host-mutant and negative-host-node-free-controls jobs exercise this instrumented host binary, built from this flake by the negative-host apps
applications/open-datum/offchain|lint|check|hosted under another name: the open-datum-component-build job runs .#lint, this same writeShellApplication derivation (apps.lint is checks.lint)
applications/open-datum/offchain|open-datum-tests|check|hosted under another name: the open-datum-tests job runs the open-datum-tests app, the same fixture-staged runner this check executes in its sandbox
applications/open-datum/onchain|open-datum-aiken-tests|app|hosted under another name: the application-aiken-suite job's nix flake check builds checks.open-datum-aiken-tests, which executes this app's runner inside the check derivation
release-review|check|app|pending wiring: #565, the release-archive slice hosts the archive reproduction job
release-review|default|app|pending wiring: #565, the release-archive slice hosts the archive reproduction job
